## Readme ##
This Utility is used to Dockerized the 'Configurations' repositories.
- It takes 'configuration.zip' as input while creating the docker-image
- Upon running this as docker-container, it carries out below tasks
    -  Unzipping Configuration Zip 
    -  Git clone the config repo from git-server 
    - Cleans intermediate folders
    - Renames Configuration Zip with timestamps
    - Setting git config
        -   user.email "gitserver@honeywell.com"
        -   config user.name "gitserver"
    -  Commit and push configrations to config repo #


## Starting GIT SERVER ##
- Checkout https://bitbucket.intellig.local/projects/RPS/repos/config-git-server/browse
- Run 'start-self-docker.sh'

## Configuration setup -- below is an example, please change values as per the underlying environment ##
docker run --rm --name config \
-v /Users/h265231/Documents/devops/reds-platform/config_mount:/opt/config-repos/config-dir \
-e GITHOST="10.79.194.245" \
configs:0.0.1;